      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5ecd03b68c8024390fb9eb0a",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 13
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With the new UI coming soon, I think it's finally time to include this as an option.\nA key motivation I see for allowing this feature, is to remove the biggest motivation currently existing for players to seek out 3rd party mods and clients. Whilst modes that allow interplayer collision are 100% harmless and non malicious, the simple act of looking into and installing these mods brings players closer to the side of things that includes malicious or intrusive modifications. It normalises the concept of using such things as standard, and makes for a slippery slope of players finding it easier to justify adding additional potentially abusable abilities that they shouldn't have.\nI've seen plenty of evidence of this myself. People who initially only wanted or cared about dynamic bone collision, gradually adding more and more, skirting the line of malicious use, and further publicly advertising in game how to acquire such things. \nThe less harmless features are officially provided, the less incentive there will be to explore potentially harmful features or uncontrollable modification.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
