      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Honestly while I understand that the devs don't want to do this because of performance issues I don't see why it couldn't be an option that you can toggle on. Even provide a small dialog box the first time you click it basically warning you that can cause performance issues. \nOther games like neos and chill out VR have already proven that this as possible. And fans absolutely love it. and pretty much everyone I know in vrchat who has a client has dynamic bone interaction as one of the main reasons they use it. The fact that this isn't already in the base game is rather surprising to me.\nthere's already clients that can toggle this on and can even be toggled for individual users. So the fact that the devs still refuse to implement this is just appalling. If a bunch of random players can slap together a way to make it work and perform reasonably well then surely the games developers could make something even better",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
